#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Enable the following options in the kernel configuration and recompile the "
"kernel if necessary:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:110
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Select the appropriate sub-options that appear when the above options are "
"selected. As much as possible, the layout should be the same as in kernel "
"configuration menus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:116
#, xml-text
msgid "Power-profiles-daemon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:121
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Power-profiles-daemon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:124
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Power-profiles-daemon</application> by running the "
"following commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:127
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup                        \\\n"
"      --prefix=/usr                \\\n"
"      --buildtype=release          \\\n"
"      -D gtk_doc=false             \\\n"
"      -D tests=false               \\\n"
"      -D systemdsystemunitdir=/tmp \\\n"
"      .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:140
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>mkdir build &amp;&amp;\n"
"cd build &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"meson setup                \\\n"
"      --prefix=/usr        \\\n"
"      --buildtype=release  \\\n"
"      -D gtk_doc=false     \\\n"
"      -D tests=false       \\\n"
"      .. &amp;&amp;\n"
"ninja</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:152
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have installed the external dependencies, to test the results issue: "
"<command> ninja test</command>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:157
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:160
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>ninja install</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:163
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, clean up an unneeded systemd unit installed into /tmp:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:167
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>rm -fv /tmp/power-profiles-daemon.service</userinput>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:171
#, xml-text
msgid "Create a directory required for persistent power states after reboot:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:176
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>install -vdm755 /var/lib/power-profiles-daemon</userinput>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:183
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:186
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D gtk_doc=false</parameter>: Prevents building the "
"documentation. Remove this if you have <application>GTK-Doc</application> "
"installed and wish to build the documentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:192
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D tests=false</parameter>: Prevents building the tests because "
"they cannot be run within the boundaries of BLFS.  Remove this if you have "
"installed the external dependencies and wish to run the tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:199
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>-D systemdsystemunitdir=/tmp</parameter>: Removes the dependency "
"on <application>systemd</application>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:206
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Power-profiles-daemon"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:209
#, xml-text
msgid "Boot Script"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:212
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To automatically start the <command>power-profiles-daemon</command> when the"
" system is rebooted, install the <filename>/etc/rc.d/init.d/power-profiles-"
"daemon</filename> bootscript from the <xref linkend=\"bootscripts\" "
"revision=\"sysv\"/> as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:223
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install-power-profiles-daemon</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:228
#, xml-text
msgid "Systemd Unit"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:231
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To start the power-profiles-daemon on boot, enable the systemd service that "
"was installed by running the following command as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:236
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>systemctl enable power-profiles-daemon</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:240
#, xml-text
msgid "Select a Power Profile"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:243
#, xml-text
msgid "To list all supported power profiles, issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:246
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>powerprofilesctl</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:249
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To activate a power profile (for example "
"<replaceable>performance</replaceable>), issue:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:253
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>powerprofilesctl set "
"<replaceable>performance</replaceable></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:256
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Some desktop environments (for example GNOME and KDE) also provide a "
"graphical interface to interact with <command>power-profiles-"
"daemon</command> and activate a power profile."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:263
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The activated power profile is automatically stored in "
"<filename>/var/lib/power-profiles-daemon/state.ini</filename> and "
"<command>power-profiles-daemon</command> will read it out and activate it "
"again on the next boot if the <phrase revision='sysv'>bootscript is "
"installed</phrase><phrase revision='systemd'>Systemd unit is "
"enabled</phrase> as above."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><caution><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:274
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"On some older systems power-profiles-daemon will appear to install and "
"indicate correct values, but will not actually work. To check this, run "
"<userinput>cat "
"/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_driver</userinput>.  If the "
"result is not \"intel_pstate\" but instead \"intel_cpufreq\" (or similar on "
"AMD systems), then power changes must be made manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><caution><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:283
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To change power states manually, first check to see what governors are "
"available with: <userinput>cat "
"/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_available_governors</userinput>."
"  Then set the desired governor as the &root; user with:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><caution><screen>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:289
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>gov=<replaceable>performance</replaceable>\n"
"for CPUFREQ in /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy*/scaling_governor; do\n"
"  echo -n ${gov} > ${CPUFREQ}\n"
"done</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><caution><para>
#: blfs-en/blfs-git/general/sysutils/power-profiles-daemon.xml:295
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you are setting the scaling_governor to \"performance\", be careful about"
" heat and battery issues with extended use."
msgstr ""

